### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 20 - AUTH PROVIDERS, WEB SESSIONS & CSRF  (Branch P109)
###
### Covers the OAuth/OIDC discovery + web-session surface of P109:
###   - GET  /api/v1/auth/providers            (public)
###   - GET  /api/v1/auth/login/{providerId}   (public, 302 → IdP or 404)
###   - GET  /api/v1/auth/callback/{providerId} (public, 400 on bad state)
###   - POST /api/v1/auth/session/rotate        (session cookie + CSRF)
###   - POST /api/v1/auth/logout                (clears cookies)
###   - POST /api/v1/auth/session/revoke-all   (authenticated)
###
### A NEW ContainerRequestFilter (ApiKeyAuthFilter) gates everything:
###   - public:  /info, /onboarding/**, /auth/providers, /auth/login,
###              /auth/callback  (all under the /api/v1 context path)
###   - API key: X-Amsha-API-Key | cookie AMSHA_API_KEY | ?apiKey=
###   - web session: cookie AMSHA_SESSION_ID (+ X-CSRF-Token for
###     POST/PUT/DELETE) or "Bearer sess-..." in Authorization.
###   - CSRF: mutating requests with a session cookie but missing/
###     invalid X-CSRF-Token → 403 FORBIDDEN.
###
### No external IdP is configured by default, so login/callback happy
### paths are NOT automatable here — only discovery + negative paths.
### A real web session cookie is minted only by a successful OIDC/GitHub
### callback; the CSRF-positive test [S3] therefore needs that cookie.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl    = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey   = key-internal-changeme
# @ciKey      = key-ci-changeme
# @invalidKey = totally-wrong-key

# Paste a real web session cookie (from an OIDC/GitHub callback) to
# exercise the CSRF-positive path. Leave blank to skip [S3]/[S4].
# @sessionCookie = sess-PASTE_FROM_AUTH_CALLBACK
# @csrfToken     = csrf-PASTE_FROM_AUTH_CALLBACK

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P. PROVIDER DISCOVERY & OAUTH NEGATIVE PATHS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [P1] List enabled providers → 200 (JSON array; empty if none configured)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/providers

### [P2] Login with unknown provider → 404 PROVIDER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login/doesnotexist

### [P3] Login with disabled provider (oidc off by default) → 404 PROVIDER_DISABLED
###      (If AMSHA_AUTH_IDP_OIDC_ENABLED=true this returns 302 → IdP.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login/oidc

### [P4] Callback with unknown state → 400 INVALID_STATE
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/callback/oidc?code=abc&state=unknown-state-token

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S. WEB SESSION LIFECYCLE & CSRF
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [S1] Rotate with NO session cookie → 401 UNAUTHORIZED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session/rotate

### [S2] Rotate with session cookie but NO CSRF token → 403 FORBIDDEN
###      (Requires @sessionCookie from a real callback.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session/rotate
Cookie: AMSHA_SESSION_ID={{sessionCookie}}

### [S3] Rotate with valid session + CSRF → 204 (new cookies set)
###      (Requires @sessionCookie and @csrfToken from a real callback.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session/rotate
Cookie: AMSHA_SESSION_ID={{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

### [S4] Logout with NO cookie → 200 (idempotent; clears cookies)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### [S5] Logout with session cookie → 200 (revokes session, clears cookies)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Cookie: AMSHA_SESSION_ID={{sessionCookie}}

### [S6] Revoke-all sessions with NO auth → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session/revoke-all

### [S7] Revoke-all sessions with API key → 200 {success:true}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session/revoke-all
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}
